From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Bradburne <abradburne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:20:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] init: open the console after mounting root

console_on_rootfs() opens /dev/console before the root file system is
mounted and takes console_lock to do so. fbcon holds that lock while its
takeover's modeset powers the panels on, so on the RG DS+ the root mount
waited for both screens to come up (~0.33 s of panel sequence).

Open the console after prepare_namespace() instead: the mount (~85 ms
with rootfstype=ext4) now overlaps the panels, and init starts when fbcon
lets go of the console, 0.66-0.72 s into the kernel.

Upstream status: board-specific hack, not for upstream. It changes when
/dev/console exists for every system, which an initramfs-less boot of
this one board doesn't need but others may.
---
 init/main.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/main.c b/init/main.c
index 31f2bf549..7213df1c9 100644
--- a/init/main.c
+++ b/init/main.c
@@ -1677,7 +1677,6 @@ static noinline void __init kernel_init_freeable(void)
 	kunit_run_all_tests();
 
 	wait_for_initramfs();
-	console_on_rootfs();
 
 	/*
 	 * check if there is an early userspace init.  If yes, let it do all
@@ -1693,6 +1692,14 @@ static noinline void __init kernel_init_freeable(void)
 		prepare_namespace();
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * After the root mount, not before: opening the console takes
+	 * console_lock, which fbcon holds while its takeover powers the panels
+	 * on. Opened first, it kept the root file system from being mounted
+	 * until the screens were up; now the mount overlaps them.
+	 */
+	console_on_rootfs();
+
 	/*
 	 * Ok, we have completed the initial bootup, and
 	 * we're essentially up and running. Get rid of the

